rapidocr provides CMake targets:

    find_package(unofficial-rapidocr CONFIG REQUIRED)
    target_link_libraries(main PRIVATE unofficial::rapidocr::rapidocr)

This port packages the C++ library RapidOcrOnnx (snapshot 2024-10-22), not
the Python RapidOCR project at https://github.com/RapidAI/RapidOCR.

Two interfaces are installed under include/rapidocr/:

  * The C++ API (#include <rapidocr/OcrLite.h>) exposes cv::Mat and other
    OpenCV types, so it must be consumed through the CMake target above, which
    propagates OpenCV's include directory. It does not resolve from the triplet
    include root alone, because OpenCV itself is installed under include/opencv4.

  * The C API (#include <rapidocr/OcrLiteCApi.h>) is a C header (extern "C"
    when compiled as C++) with no OpenCV types, so it can be consumed from C
    or C++ with only the triplet include root on the search path.

On Windows a shared build of this port uses dllimport in the C API header.
A static build defines RAPIDOCR_STATIC on the imported target so the header
does not use a storage class.

The recognition dictionary is installed with the port:

    ${CURRENT_INSTALLED_DIR}/share/rapidocr/models/ppocr_keys_v1.txt

The ONNX model weights are not redistributed and must be obtained separately:

    ch_PP-OCRv3_det_infer.onnx
    ch_PP-OCRv3_rec_infer.onnx
    ch_ppocr_mobile_v2.0_cls_infer.onnx

See https://github.com/RapidAI/RapidOcrOnnx for details.
